    "title": "New-look Buccaneers ready to change the narrative - NewsBreak",
    "text": "LYNN HAVEN, Fla. (WMBB) – The struggles faced by the North Bay Haven football program have been no secret in recent years. But as a new season approaches, the team believes the story is about to change. The Buccaneers closed last year without a win, finishing 0-10. However, assistant coach Trenton Edwards says the film from this summer’s practices, has been viewed as a sign of progression. In the spring, head coach Andy Siegal took over the program and brought in a new line up of veteran coaches, creating a more structured environment. “It just feels more like it feels like a program now instead of a club,” senior running back Jackson Shoults said. The coaching additions have attracted more athletes onto the field, including multi-sport standouts have also been integrated into the roster. Over the past year, changing the culture around the football program has been a top priority. Players have said the energy in practice is markedly different from one year ago. With last season serving as motivation, the Buccaneers believe a stronger and more competitive team will take the field this fall. North Bay Haven will open its season at Freeport on Friday, Aug. 22. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to mypanhandle.com.",
